      "id": 1,
      "text": "Swedish pioneers settled around 1867 in what became Old Kiron, establishing a rural community in Crawford County.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/kiron_iowa",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Chicago and North Western Railway built the Mondamin branch line through Crawford County, prompting Kiron's establishment at its current location in 1899.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/kiron_iowa",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Kiron's name came from a misspelled Kidron Valley, with the \"D\" omitted during early settlement.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kiron%2C_Iowa",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The town became the first station west of Boyer, enabling efficient shipment of local grain, livestock, and farm produce to broader markets.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/kiron_iowa",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Kiron's modest median household income of $50,781 in 2022 reflects its agrarian focus, with residents keeping traditions like coffee socials and council governance in a 100% rural setting.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        28
